/*!
  \page example_cu_knngraph_page Fitting with k-NN graph queries in CUDA kernels

  This example is the counterpart of \ref example_cu_kdtree_page with a Ponca::KnnGraph: the graph is built on the
  CPU from a kd-tree, its buffers are copied to the device, and the kernel queries it to collect the neighbors of
  each point before fitting a plane.

  To compile and run the example:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target cuda_fit_plane_knngraph
  ./build/examples/cuda/cuda_fit_plane_knngraph
  \endcode

  See also \ref ponca_gpu_spatial.

  \include cuda/ponca_fit_knngraph.cu
 */
